        "reading": {
          "text": "Edition J keeps two columns. Inherited account: two separate lower-jaw bones. Specimen J: adult human, continuous bone across the chin. Editorial correction: use the specimen-supported account here and retain the displaced wording in the record. This applies the earlier practice of preserving a variant while repairing a claim; the old C/D triangle proof contributes no anatomical observation.",
          "attribution": "Authored historical teaching case, not an original quotation or an actual specimen record."
        }
